_:r3dafcfbc12d24a546d5cd233_n8f98698f37cb4d92b790bb0819b9e2cbb10 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/description_html> .
_:r3dafcfbc12d24a546d5cd233_n8f98698f37cb4d92b790bb0819b9e2cbb10 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:r3dafcfbc12d24a546d5cd233_n8f98698f37cb4d92b790bb0819b9e2cbb10 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "<p> Localizing a functional region usually means running a dedicated localizer. This asks whether the same regions can be found in data that was rich to begin with -- a feature film, watched once -- and reports that a GLM is the wrong tool for it. Dormant; worth returning to. </p> <ul> <li> A. Wagner, S. Nastase, Y.O. Halchenko and M. Hanke (2019). <a href=\"https://juser.fz-juelich.de/record/865045/files/OHBM_2019_Wagner.pdf\">Functional ROI localization in a rich stimuli dataset requires non-GLM style approach</a>. OHBM 2019, Rome, Italy. </li> <li> S.A. Nastase, J.S. Guntupalli, <a href=\"/whoweare#james_v_haxby_\" class=\"centroid\">J.V. Haxby</a> and <a href=\"/whoweare#yaroslav_o_halchenko_\" class=\"centroid\">Y.O. Halchenko</a> (2016). Localizing functional regions of interest based on responses to dynamic naturalistic stimuli. SfN 2016, San Diego. </li> <li> <a href=\"/whoweare#matteo_visconti_di_oleggio_castello_\" class=\"centroid\">M. Visconti di Oleggio Castello</a>, S.A. Nastase, M.I. Gobbini, <a href=\"/whoweare#james_v_haxby_\" class=\"centroid\">J.V. Haxby</a> and <a href=\"/whoweare#yaroslav_o_halchenko_\" class=\"centroid\">Y.O. Halchenko</a> (2015). Finding Cortical Patches of Shared Representations. SfN 2015, Chicago, Poster 451.11. </li> </ul>" .
