_:rbb2ab5c95963f401888f8e7d_n991f4cd2b6e54de3ab7b8b7cffd011c7b15 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/description_html> .
_:rbb2ab5c95963f401888f8e7d_n991f4cd2b6e54de3ab7b8b7cffd011c7b15 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:rbb2ab5c95963f401888f8e7d_n991f4cd2b6e54de3ab7b8b7cffd011c7b15 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "<p> <a href=\"https://github.com/con/fscacher\">con/fscacher</a> is a Python library providing a persistent, file-content-aware memoization cache. Functions decorated with <code>@cache.memoize_path</code> are re-executed only when the fingerprint (timestamps + size) of their file arguments changes — making it easy to cache expensive operations on large file trees without stale results. It is used internally by the <a href=\"#dandi\">DANDI</a> client and other CON tools. </p>" .
