_:rc89a26e4e5ef9b7f15952ef4_n914c0c39744a433cad0c9f49985257e0b5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "Senior Research Scientist (Directrice de recherche), Inria, Empenn team, Rennes" .
_:rc89a26e4e5ef9b7f15952ef4_n914c0c39744a433cad0c9f49985257e0b6 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/description_html> .
_:rc89a26e4e5ef9b7f15952ef4_n914c0c39744a433cad0c9f49985257e0b6 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:rc89a26e4e5ef9b7f15952ef4_n914c0c39744a433cad0c9f49985257e0b6 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "Studies neuroimaging reproducibility, and in particular the variability that analytical pipelines introduce and its impact on reusing brain imaging data. A member of the <a href=\"/projects#brain_imaging_data_structure_bids_\">BIDS</a> Steering Group, the lead of <a href=\"/projects#bep028_\">BEP028</a> (BIDS provenance), and the principal developer of NIDM-Results within <a href=\"/projects#nidm_\">NIDM</a>. The collaboration began at the INCF Neuroimaging Data Sharing Task Force meeting in San Diego in November 2013, and runs through NIDM, BIDS and its provenance extension, and the <a href=\"/projects#open_brain_consent_\">Open Brain Consent</a>, which she helped translate into French." .
_:rca58d40f250521d52d078477_nfab65f341b5b44398d822f6aef985190b1 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/Identifier> .
