_:re633d6602d696416154e8a7b_n00217d077e9a484585d03cf3de7a5143b5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "MRI Phantoms Afterlife" .
_:re633d6602d696416154e8a7b_n00217d077e9a484585d03cf3de7a5143b6 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> .
_:re633d6602d696416154e8a7b_n00217d077e9a484585d03cf3de7a5143b6 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:re633d6602d696416154e8a7b_n00217d077e9a484585d03cf3de7a5143b6 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "Scanner QA data is acquired to watch the scanner, and then it is filed away. This asks what else it is good for -- whether the variance in routine phantom scans explains variance in the human data acquired around them, which would make years of accumulated QA scans a covariate rather than a formality." .
_:re633d6602d696416154e8a7b_n00217d077e9a484585d03cf3de7a5143b7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> .
_:re633d6602d696416154e8a7b_n00217d077e9a484585d03cf3de7a5143b7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:re633d6602d696416154e8a7b_n00217d077e9a484585d03cf3de7a5143b7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "MRI Phantoms Afterlife" .
_:re633d6602d696416154e8a7b_n00217d077e9a484585d03cf3de7a5143b8 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/description_html> .
_:re633d6602d696416154e8a7b_n00217d077e9a484585d03cf3de7a5143b8 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:re633d6602d696416154e8a7b_n00217d077e9a484585d03cf3de7a5143b8 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "<p> Scanner QA data is acquired to watch the scanner, and then it is filed away. This asks what else it is good for -- whether the variance in routine phantom scans explains variance in the human data acquired around them, which would make years of accumulated QA scans a covariate rather than a formality. It runs on <a href=\"https://github.com/dbic/QA\">dbic/QA</a>, the phantom, human and LEGO scans <a href=\"https://datasets.datalad.org/?dir=/dbic/QA\">collected at DBIC</a>. </p> <ul> <li> C.P. Cheng and <a href=\"/whoweare#yaroslav_o_halchenko_\" class=\"centroid\">Y.O. Halchenko</a> (2020). <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.12688/f1000research.24544.1\">A new virtue of phantom MRI data: explaining variance in human participant data</a>. F1000Research, 9:1131. </li> </ul>" .
_:re633d6602d696416154e8a7b_n00217d077e9a484585d03cf3de7a5143b9 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/short_name> .
_:re633d6602d696416154e8a7b_n00217d077e9a484585d03cf3de7a5143b9 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:re633d6602d696416154e8a7b_n00217d077e9a484585d03cf3de7a5143b9 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "MRI Phantoms Afterlife" .
_:re64b9a09dfc41dd689f8c641_n5b7fb58c7a554422a5df443ca8a73c95b1 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> .
