_:rf4a1adf7eeb8a41a162ab308_ncf77de6c76df42498ffab25e042b7915b11 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> .
_:rf4a1adf7eeb8a41a162ab308_ncf77de6c76df42498ffab25e042b7915b11 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:rf4a1adf7eeb8a41a162ab308_ncf77de6c76df42498ffab25e042b7915b11 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "con/tributors is a Python library and GitHub Action to automate maintenance of contributor attribution files. It updates all-contributors, Zenodo metadata (.zenodo.json), and CodeMeta (codemeta.json) files in one go, using a shared .tributors cache that maps GitHub logins to ORCID iDs and other persistent identifiers — so that contributor records stay consistent and up-to-date across all metadata files with a single command. For example, DataLad uses a dedicated GitHub Actions workflow powered by con/tributors to automatically keep its contributor files current." .
_:rf4a1adf7eeb8a41a162ab308_ncf77de6c76df42498ffab25e042b7915b12 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/section> .
_:rf4a1adf7eeb8a41a162ab308_ncf77de6c76df42498ffab25e042b7915b12 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:rf4a1adf7eeb8a41a162ab308_ncf77de6c76df42498ffab25e042b7915b12 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "Software" .
_:rf4a1adf7eeb8a41a162ab308_ncf77de6c76df42498ffab25e042b7915b13 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/description_html> .
_:rf4a1adf7eeb8a41a162ab308_ncf77de6c76df42498ffab25e042b7915b13 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:rf4a1adf7eeb8a41a162ab308_ncf77de6c76df42498ffab25e042b7915b13 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "<p> <a href=\"https://github.com/con/tributors\">con/tributors</a> is a Python library and GitHub Action to automate maintenance of contributor attribution files. It updates <a href=\"https://allcontributors.org\">all-contributors</a>, <a href=\"https://zenodo.org\">Zenodo</a> metadata (.zenodo.json), and <a href=\"https://codemeta.github.io/\">CodeMeta</a> (codemeta.json) files in one go, using a shared <code>.tributors</code> cache that maps GitHub logins to ORCID iDs and other persistent identifiers — so that contributor records stay consistent and up-to-date across all metadata files with a single command. For example, DataLad uses a <a href=\"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/master/.github/workflows/update-contributors.yml\">dedicated GitHub Actions workflow</a> powered by con/tributors to automatically keep its contributor files current. </p>" .
_:rf4a1adf7eeb8a41a162ab308_ncf77de6c76df42498ffab25e042b7915b14 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/Start> .
